[size=6]Vault 106[/size]
[size=4]
Vault 106 is a Dwemer town built into the side of a mountain near Markarth. Visit this repopulated Dwarven settlement and have some Nuka-Mead, the Overseer will be watching. Inspired by Vault 101 & 106 from Fallout 3.

All vault dwellers have daily routines, they will operate their shops or perform vault maintenance by day, and drink Nuka-Mead in the tavern or atrium at night. The youths will learn about the almighty G.O.A.T. on weekdays.

The 'outsider quarters' is an apartment for the dragonborn, it is available upon arrival without purchase to allow easier updates for ESL users.

Requires Dragonborn DLC.

[size=5]Development[/size]
This mod is a continuation of the Vault 101 Skyrim mod. Notable changes include: improved vault layout, added apartments for all dwellers, added dweller schedules and packages, ported to Skyrim SE, and optimized to support ESL.

More features will be added in future updates including additional dweller package improvements, and adding 'the experiment' of Vault 106.

Suggestions and requests are always welcome.

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*] Navigate to C:/Program Files (x86)/Steam/SteamApps/common/Skyrim/ (or wherever you have Skyrim installed on your system).
[*] Merge the Data folder from the mod’s zip file with the Data folder in the Skyrim directory.
[*] Launch Skyrim and click on 'Data Files', then make sure the mod is enabled. Enjoy!
[/list]
[/size]

